Pick LFG fill bots by the role the group is still missing, record the role they
actually play instead of a flat DAMAGE, and make the missing roles exist.
Touches: modules/mod-playerbots/src/Bot/RandomPlayerbotMgr.cpp and .h --
FillLfgRaidGroup(), EnsureQueueFillBots(), plus new EnsureLfgRoleBots(),
RetargetBotToBand() and LoginExtraBotsForRole()
Applies on top of 0003-playerbot-lfg-role.core-patch (same function, same lines).

Why: FillLfgRaidGroup() selected bots on team, level range and idle flag and
nothing else, so a bot-filled dungeon group was whichever four idle bots the
map iterated first. No tank, no healer, no guarantee of either -- whether the
run was viable came down to the luck of their specs. Patch 0003 then stamped
every one of them PLAYER_ROLE_DAMAGE, which was only ever about giving the
proposal packet something the client could render.

This fills to a shape instead. Each pass asks for the role the group still
needs -- 1 tank and 1 healer for a 5-man, 2 tanks and a healer per 5 bodies for
a raid fill -- and takes the first idle bot that plays it, counting the real
players already in the group so a player who queued as tank isn't handed a
second one. If no idle bot can fill the role, it falls back to any eligible bot
rather than leaving the group a body short.

The role each bot actually plays now goes onto its group member slot
(Group::AddMember's roles argument, which drives the party-frame role icon) as
well as into LFG's player data, so nothing downstream sees a bot whose recorded
role is a lie. Role detection is PlayerbotAI::IsTank/IsHeal, which reads a bot's
own active strategy and falls back to spec and class -- the same path real party
members resolve through, since they have no bot AI to ask.

Shaping the fill is only half of it, because it can only pick from bots that
already exist. The second half makes them exist. EnsureQueueFillBots() already
ran a periodic pass that retargeted idle bots into the level band real players
were queueing for; it now also makes sure that band actually contains a tank and
a healer for the faction in question, trying three things in order of cost:

  1. Respec an idle bot that is already at the right level and whose class can
     play the role (talents first, then gear -- InitEquipment picks for whatever
     spec the bot has when it runs).
  2. Retarget an idle bot of a capable class into the level band, then respec it.
  3. Log extra bots in, deliberately bypassing AddRandomBots()' bot_count cap: a
     queue short a tank is short a tank whether or not the realm is at its
     configured bot count. They are ordinary random bots once in world, so the
     usual in-world timer logs them out again and the population settles itself.

Spec templates are matched by keyword against the playerbots.conf
AiPlayerbot.PremadeSpecName.* names ("prot pve", "bear pve", "resto pve" ...)
and the result is then verified against the bot's real role, so a renamed or
reordered template costs a retry rather than producing a wrong bot.

The role pass runs after the existing retargeting so bots pulled into the band
on this same tick are candidates, and only for LFG brackets -- battlegrounds
don't care which role turns up.

--- a/modules/mod-playerbots/src/Bot/RandomPlayerbotMgr.cpp
+++ b/modules/mod-playerbots/src/Bot/RandomPlayerbotMgr.cpp
@@ (above IsIdleFillBot)
+// The role a player would actually fill in a dungeon: the bot's own active
+// strategy where it has one, spec and class otherwise -- which is also what real
+// party members resolve through, since they have no bot AI to ask.
+static uint8 LfgFillRoleOf(Player* player)
+{
+    if (PlayerbotAI::IsTank(player))
+        return lfg::PLAYER_ROLE_TANK;
+
+    if (PlayerbotAI::IsHeal(player))
+        return lfg::PLAYER_ROLE_HEALER;
+
+    return lfg::PLAYER_ROLE_DAMAGE;
+}
+
 static bool IsIdleFillBot(Player* bot)
 {
@@ RandomPlayerbotMgr::FillLfgRaidGroup(Group* group, uint32 maxPlayers, uint8 minLevel, uint8 maxLevel)
     TeamId const team = leader->GetTeamId();
-    uint32 added = 0;
+
+    // What the group still needs, so the fill doesn't hand a player four random
+    // idle bots and no tank or healer. 5-man is the LFG 1/1/3; a raid fill gets
+    // two tanks and a healer per five bodies, roughly the shape 10s and 25s run.
+    uint32 const tanksWanted = maxPlayers <= MAXGROUPSIZE ? 1 : 2;
+    uint32 const healersWanted = maxPlayers <= MAXGROUPSIZE ? 1 : std::max<uint32>(2, maxPlayers / 5);
+
+    uint32 tanks = 0;
+    uint32 healers = 0;
+    for (GroupReference* itr = group->GetFirstMember(); itr != nullptr; itr = itr->next())
+    {
+        if (Player* member = itr->GetSource())
+        {
+            uint8 const role = LfgFillRoleOf(member);
+            if (role == lfg::PLAYER_ROLE_TANK)
+                ++tanks;
+            else if (role == lfg::PLAYER_ROLE_HEALER)
+                ++healers;
+        }
+    }
+
+    uint32 added = 0;
     while (group->GetMembersCount() < maxPlayers)
     {
+        uint8 const wanted = tanks < tanksWanted      ? lfg::PLAYER_ROLE_TANK
+                             : healers < healersWanted ? lfg::PLAYER_ROLE_HEALER
+                                                       : lfg::PLAYER_ROLE_DAMAGE;
+
         Player* bot = nullptr;
+        Player* fallback = nullptr;
         for (auto const& pair : playerBots)
         {
             Player* candidate = pair.second;
             if (!IsRandomBot(candidate) || !IsIdleFillBot(candidate))
                 continue;
             if (candidate->GetTeamId() != team)
                 continue;
             uint32 const level = candidate->GetLevel();
             if (level < minLevel || level > maxLevel)
                 continue;
             if (group->IsMember(candidate->GetGUID()))
                 continue;
-            bot = candidate;
-            break;
+
+            if (LfgFillRoleOf(candidate) == wanted)
+            {
+                bot = candidate;
+                break;
+            }
+
+            if (!fallback)
+                fallback = candidate;
         }
+
+        // Nobody idle can fill the role we wanted -- a full group of the wrong
+        // shape still beats leaving the player short a body
+        if (!bot)
+            bot = fallback;
         if (!bot)
             break;
@@ (member insertion, replacing 0003's flat DAMAGE role)
-        if (!group->AddMember(bot))
-            break;
-        // Bots added this way skip the normal LFG queue/role-check flow
-        // entirely, so their LFG role stays PLAYER_ROLE_NONE. [...]
-        // A flat DAMAGE role here is just for that packet/icon --
-        // it doesn't affect the bot's actual combat AI role.
-        sLFGMgr->SetRoles(bot->GetGUID(), lfg::PLAYER_ROLE_DAMAGE);
+        // Bots added this way skip the normal LFG queue/role-check flow entirely,
+        // so nothing else ever gives them an LFG role. Record the one they will
+        // actually play, both on the group member slot (the party-frame role
+        // icon) and in LFG's own player data -- a roleless member used to reach
+        // the client as PLAYER_ROLE_NONE and throw Lua errors there.
+        uint8 const role = LfgFillRoleOf(bot);
+        if (!group->AddMember(bot, role))
+            break;
+        sLFGMgr->SetRoles(bot->GetGUID(), role);
+
+        if (role == lfg::PLAYER_ROLE_TANK)
+            ++tanks;
+        else if (role == lfg::PLAYER_ROLE_HEALER)
+            ++healers;
+
         ++added;
     }

     if (added)
-        LOG_INFO("playerbots", "Filled LFG raid group with {} bots ({}/{})", added, group->GetMembersCount(), maxPlayers);
+        LOG_INFO("playerbots", "Filled LFG raid group with {} bots ({}/{}, {} tanks, {} healers)", added,
+                 group->GetMembersCount(), maxPlayers, tanks, healers);

--- a/modules/mod-playerbots/src/Bot/RandomPlayerbotMgr.h
+++ b/modules/mod-playerbots/src/Bot/RandomPlayerbotMgr.h
@@ (near EnsureQueueFillBots)
     void EnsureQueueFillBots();
+    // Make sure a tank and a healer exist for LFG demand in a level band, by
+    // respec, by retarget, or by logging extra bots in over the configured cap
+    void EnsureLfgRoleBots(TeamId team, uint32 minLevel, uint32 maxLevel);
+    bool RetargetBotToBand(Player* bot, uint32 minLevel, uint32 maxLevel);
+    uint32 LoginExtraBotsForRole(TeamId team, uint8 role, uint32 count);
     void FillLfgRaidGroup(Group* group, uint32 maxPlayers, uint8 minLevel, uint8 maxLevel);

--- a/modules/mod-playerbots/src/Bot/RandomPlayerbotMgr.cpp
+++ b/modules/mod-playerbots/src/Bot/RandomPlayerbotMgr.cpp
@@ (above IsIdleFillBot, after LfgFillRoleOf)
+// Classes with the talents to fill a role at all, so we never try to convert a
+// bot that could never play it.
+static bool ClassCanFillRole(uint8 cls, uint8 role)
+{
+    if (role == lfg::PLAYER_ROLE_TANK)
+        return cls == CLASS_WARRIOR || cls == CLASS_PALADIN || cls == CLASS_DRUID || cls == CLASS_DEATH_KNIGHT;
+
+    return cls == CLASS_PALADIN || cls == CLASS_PRIEST || cls == CLASS_DRUID || cls == CLASS_SHAMAN;
+}
+
+// Premade spec templates are named in playerbots.conf ("prot pve", "bear pve",
+// "resto pve" ...), so match them by keyword rather than by index. Whatever this
+// picks is verified against the bot's real role afterwards, so a renamed or
+// reordered template costs a retry rather than producing a wrong bot.
+static bool SpecNameFitsRole(std::string const& name, uint8 role)
+{
+    auto has = [&name](char const* word) { return name.find(word) != std::string::npos; };
+
+    if (role == lfg::PLAYER_ROLE_TANK)
+        return has("prot") || has("blood") || has("bear");
+
+    return has("holy") || has("disc") || has("resto");
+}
+
+// Respec an idle bot into a role the queue is short of. Talents first and gear
+// second, because InitEquipment picks for whatever spec the bot has when it runs.
+static bool RespecBotForRole(Player* bot, uint8 role)
+{
+    PlayerbotAI* botAI = GET_PLAYERBOT_AI(bot);
+    if (!botAI)
+        return false;
+
+    uint32 const cls = bot->getClass();
+    for (int specNo = 0; specNo < MAX_SPECNO; ++specNo)
+    {
+        std::string const& name = sPlayerbotAIConfig.premadeSpecName[cls][specNo];
+        if (name.empty())
+            break;
+        // PvE templates only -- a PvP build makes a worse dungeon tank
+        if (name.find("pvp") != std::string::npos || !SpecNameFitsRole(name, role))
+            continue;
+
+        PlayerbotFactory::InitTalentsBySpecNo(bot, specNo, true);
+
+        PlayerbotFactory factory(bot, bot->GetLevel());
+        factory.InitEquipment(false);
+        botAI->Reset(true);
+
+        if (LfgFillRoleOf(bot) == role)
+        {
+            LOG_INFO("playerbots", "Respecced bot {} to '{}' to cover an LFG role", bot->GetName(), name);
+            return true;
+        }
+    }
+
+    return false;
+}
+
 static bool IsIdleFillBot(Player* bot)
 {
@@ RandomPlayerbotMgr::EnsureQueueFillBots() -- bracket bookkeeping
     std::vector<BracketNeed> needs;
+
+    // LFG brackets only: battlegrounds don't care which role turns up
+    struct RoleBracket
+    {
+        TeamId team;
+        uint32 minLevel;
+        uint32 maxLevel;
+    };
+    std::vector<RoleBracket> lfgBrackets;

@@ RandomPlayerbotMgr::EnsureQueueFillBots() -- addLfgNeed lambda
             needs.push_back(need);
+            lfgBrackets.push_back({team, minLevel, maxLevel});
         };

@@ RandomPlayerbotMgr::EnsureQueueFillBots() -- end of the retarget loop
         retargetList(idleAlliance, need.allianceNeed);
         retargetList(idleHorde, need.hordeNeed);
     }
+
+    // Bodies are not enough on their own -- five dps is a wipe. Do this after the
+    // retargeting above so bots just pulled into the band count as candidates.
+    for (RoleBracket const& bracket : lfgBrackets)
+        EnsureLfgRoleBots(bracket.team, bracket.minLevel, bracket.maxLevel);
 }
+
+void RandomPlayerbotMgr::EnsureLfgRoleBots(TeamId team, uint32 minLevel, uint32 maxLevel)
+{
+    // One of each is what a 5-man needs; everything past that is dps, which is
+    // what the ordinary fill produces anyway.
+    uint8 const roles[2] = {lfg::PLAYER_ROLE_TANK, lfg::PLAYER_ROLE_HEALER};
+
+    for (uint8 role : roles)
+    {
+        std::vector<Player*> convertible;   // idle, right level, could play the role
+        std::vector<Player*> retargetable;  // idle, wrong level, could play the role
+        bool covered = false;
+
+        for (auto const& pair : playerBots)
+        {
+            Player* bot = pair.second;
+            if (!IsRandomBot(bot) || !IsIdleFillBot(bot) || bot->GetTeamId() != team)
+                continue;
+
+            uint32 const level = bot->GetLevel();
+            bool const inBand = level >= minLevel && level <= maxLevel;
+            if (inBand && LfgFillRoleOf(bot) == role)
+            {
+                covered = true;
+                break;
+            }
+
+            if (ClassCanFillRole(bot->getClass(), role))
+                (inBand ? convertible : retargetable).push_back(bot);
+        }
+
+        if (covered)
+            continue;
+
+        // Cheapest first: an idle bot already at the right level only needs a respec
+        for (Player* bot : convertible)
+        {
+            if (RespecBotForRole(bot, role))
+            {
+                covered = true;
+                break;
+            }
+        }
+
+        // Then: pull an idle bot into the level band and respec that
+        for (Player* bot : retargetable)
+        {
+            if (covered)
+                break;
+            if (RetargetBotToBand(bot, minLevel, maxLevel) && RespecBotForRole(bot, role))
+                covered = true;
+        }
+
+        // Still nothing: log more in and convert them on a later pass, once they
+        // are actually in world
+        if (!covered && !LoginExtraBotsForRole(team, role, 2))
+            LOG_INFO("playerbots", "No bot available to cover the LFG {} shortage for levels {}-{}",
+                     role == lfg::PLAYER_ROLE_TANK ? "tank" : "healer", minLevel, maxLevel);
+    }
+}
+
+bool RandomPlayerbotMgr::RetargetBotToBand(Player* bot, uint32 minLevel, uint32 maxLevel)
+{
+    PlayerbotAI* botAI = GET_PLAYERBOT_AI(bot);
+    if (!botAI)
+        return false;
+
+    uint32 level = urand(minLevel, maxLevel);
+    if (bot->getClass() == CLASS_DEATH_KNIGHT)
+    {
+        uint32 const dkMin = sWorld->getIntConfig(CONFIG_START_HEROIC_PLAYER_LEVEL);
+        if (level < dkMin)
+        {
+            if (maxLevel < dkMin)
+                return false;
+            level = urand(dkMin, maxLevel);
+        }
+    }
+
+    SetValue(bot, "level", level);
+    PlayerbotFactory factory(bot, level);
+    factory.Randomize(false);
+    botAI->Reset(true);
+    if (bot->GetGroup())
+        botAI->LeaveOrDisbandGroup();
+
+    return true;
+}
+
+uint32 RandomPlayerbotMgr::LoginExtraBotsForRole(TeamId team, uint8 role, uint32 count)
+{
+    if (!count || rndBotTypeAccounts.empty())
+        return 0;
+
+    std::vector<uint32> accounts = rndBotTypeAccounts;
+    std::shuffle(accounts.begin(), accounts.end(),
+                 std::mt19937(std::chrono::steady_clock::now().time_since_epoch().count()));
+
+    uint32 queued = 0;
+    for (uint32 accountId : accounts)
+    {
+        if (queued >= count)
+            break;
+
+        CharacterDatabasePreparedStatement* stmt = CharacterDatabase.GetPreparedStatement(CHAR_SEL_CHARS_BY_ACCOUNT_ID);
+        stmt->SetData(0, accountId);
+        PreparedQueryResult result = CharacterDatabase.Query(stmt);
+        if (!result)
+            continue;
+
+        do
+        {
+            Field* fields = result->Fetch();
+            uint32 const guid = fields[0].Get<uint32>();
+            uint8 const rClass = fields[1].Get<uint8>();
+            uint8 const rRace = fields[2].Get<uint8>();
+
+            if (!ClassCanFillRole(rClass, role))
+                continue;
+            if ((IsAlliance(rRace) ? TEAM_ALLIANCE : TEAM_HORDE) != team)
+                continue;
+            if (sPlayerbotAIConfig.disableDeathKnightLogin && rClass == CLASS_DEATH_KNIGHT)
+                continue;
+            if (GetEventValue(guid, "add") || GetEventValue(guid, "logout") || GetPlayerBot(guid) ||
+                std::find(currentBots.begin(), currentBots.end(), guid) != currentBots.end())
+                continue;
+
+            // The login recipe AddRandomBots() uses, deliberately without its
+            // bot_count ceiling: a queue short a tank is short a tank whether or
+            // not we are at the configured cap. These are ordinary random bots
+            // once in world, so the usual in-world timer logs them back out and
+            // the population settles itself.
+            uint32 const addTime = sPlayerbotAIConfig.enablePeriodicOnlineOffline
+                                       ? urand(sPlayerbotAIConfig.minRandomBotInWorldTime,
+                                               sPlayerbotAIConfig.maxRandomBotInWorldTime)
+                                       : sPlayerbotAIConfig.permanentlyInWorldTime;
+            SetEventValue(guid, "add", 1, addTime);
+            SetEventValue(guid, "logout", 0, 0);
+            currentBots.push_back(guid);
+
+            if (++queued >= count)
+                break;
+        } while (result->NextRow());
+    }
+
+    if (queued)
+        LOG_INFO("playerbots", "Logging in {} extra bot(s) over the cap for an LFG {} shortage", queued,
+                 role == lfg::PLAYER_ROLE_TANK ? "tank" : "healer");
+
+    return queued;
+}
